##			- Every command now verifies repo state first and is idempotent: stash only if dirty (and pop only what was pushed), pull only with an upstream, push only if ahead, commit only if there are changes.
##			- Detect main vs master from origin's HEAD instead of a hardcoded name.
##			- Run git via argument arrays instead of eval; dropped the curly-quote message mangling (no longer needed).
##			- mtm merges --no-ff and deletes the merged branch local + remote; guards against running from the default branch.
##			- mkbranch/chbranch validate branch existence up front and park current work (commit+pull+push) before switching.
